# Demo 18 requests: open this file in VS Code with the REST Client extension
# (by Huachao Mao). A small "Send Request" link appears above each request.
# Click it and the response opens on the right: status line, headers, body.
#
# Start the server first:  npm start
# Requests are separated by lines that start with ###
# A request is:  METHOD URL    then header lines    then ONE blank line    then the body
#
# Restart the server to put the data back the way it started.

@host = http://localhost:3001

### 1. Is the server up?
GET {{host}}/api/health

### 2. The whole collection: every book (200, a JSON array)
GET {{host}}/api/books

### 3. One item: the book with id 42 (200, one JSON object)
GET {{host}}/api/books/42

### 4. An item that does not exist (404 Not Found)
GET {{host}}/api/books/999

### 5. An id that is not a number (400 Bad Request)
GET {{host}}/api/books/abc

### 6. Query string: only available books
GET {{host}}/api/books?available=true

### 7. Query string with two parameters (search + filter)
GET {{host}}/api/books?q=the&available=true

### 8. Create a book (201 Created). Look for the Location header in the response.
POST {{host}}/api/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "The Golden Compass",
  "author": "Philip Pullman",
  "year": 1995
}

### 9. Create, but forget the Content-Type header (415 Unsupported Media Type)
POST {{host}}/api/books

{ "title": "No header", "author": "Someone" }

### 10. Create with broken JSON: single quotes (400, "Invalid JSON")
POST {{host}}/api/books
Content-Type: application/json

{ 'title': 'Bad quotes', 'author': 'Someone' }

### 11. Create with valid JSON but a missing field (400, "Validation failed")
POST {{host}}/api/books
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Who wrote me?" }

### 12. PUT replaces the WHOLE book. (Book 43 is the one request 8 created.)
PUT {{host}}/api/books/43
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Northern Lights",
  "author": "Philip Pullman",
  "year": 1995,
  "available": false
}

### 13. PUT with only one field: the server says title and author are required (400)
PUT {{host}}/api/books/43
Content-Type: application/json

{ "available": true }

### 14. PATCH changes only the fields you send (200)
PATCH {{host}}/api/books/43
Content-Type: application/json

{ "available": true }

### 15. Delete it (204 No Content: success, no body)
DELETE {{host}}/api/books/43

### 16. Delete it again (404: it is already gone; the server is in the same state)
DELETE {{host}}/api/books/43

### 17. A method this URL does not support (405 Method Not Allowed; see the Allow header)
DELETE {{host}}/api/books

### 18. A redirect (301). REST Client follows it, so you may see the book list.
GET {{host}}/old-books

### 19. A server error (500)
GET {{host}}/api/broken
